// A continuous pull toward this entity's own position - see VortexSystem. The pull radius comes
// from this entity's own PhysicsCollider3D (must be a Sphere) rather than a field here - same
// reasoning AreaDamageSystem's pulse area comes from its own collider, not an authored radius. That
// also means the existing generic SpawnRadiusUpgrade (which already scales whatever collider a
// spawned entity has) works on a vortex for free, with no vortex-specific radius plumbing needed.
//
// No Damage field here on purpose - a vortex is pure crowd control by default. VortexDamageUpgrade
// adds actual damage by attaching a real AreaDamage component instead (see SpawnVortexEffectData),
// reusing AreaDamageSystem's own independent pulsing rather than hand-rolling a second damage-tick
// system on Vortex itself.
//
// Force is set at spawn by SpawnVortexEffectData.PullForce - its own baseline, decoupled from Kai's
// Cast Damage (which is dealt directly on impact instead, then becomes "Vortex Skill Damage," the
// percentage basis every Ascension line scales off - see KaiAscensionUtility.
// ResolveVortexSkillDamage). Singularity (see Heroes/Kai/Singularity.qtn) MULTIPLIES this baseline
// rather than overriding it.
component Vortex
{
    // Applied as one impulse per pulse (TickInterval/TickTimer below), not scaled by DeltaTime - a
    // continuous DeltaTime-scaled push turned out too small to read against ground friction (see
    // DamageUtility.PushPhysicsBody) and against the enemy's own chase velocity, which EnemySystem
    // reassigns every tick regardless. A periodic, full-sized pop is what actually visibly drags an
    // enemy off its chase line.
    FP Force;

    // Seconds between pull pulses - authored directly on the prototype, never overridden at spawn.
    FP TickInterval;

    FP TickTimer;

    // How many enemies the last pull pulse actually found in radius - refreshed once per pulse (not
    // every tick, to avoid an extra OverlapShape query), reusing the same overlap the pull itself
    // already runs. Read by VortexSystem.ResolveCrowdMultiplier (VortexCrowdDamageUpgrade) to scale
    // the constant AreaDamage, Implosion pulses and the final blast all off the same live count - see
    // VortexSystem.Update.
    Byte CaughtCount;
}
